From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:33:22 +0200
Subject: thermal/drivers/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5: drop IIO_VAL_INT check

Commit bb21ee31f575 changed iio_read_channel_processed_scale() to
return zero on success instead of IIO_VAL_INT. The existing check treats
valid ADC temperatures as -EINVAL and eventually disables every PMK8280
board thermal zone.

Drop the stale return-value check and rely on negative errors. This is the
upstream fix queued for Linux 7.3 and restores all eight Q8B thermistors.

Fixes: bb21ee31f575 ("iio: Fix iio_multiply_value use in iio_read_channel_processed_scale")
(cherry picked from commit 0c569e22020f53ddfac0099b0aa193907bfbcd6f)
Signed-off-by: Rakesh Kota <rakesh.kota@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Daniel Lezcano <daniel.lezcano@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Jonathan Cameron <jonathan.cameron@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260724-adc-tm5-drop-iio-val-int-check-v1-1-0b85a0895dd7@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c b/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c
@@ -369,9 +369,6 @@ static int adc_tm5_get_temp(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, int *temp)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (ret != IIO_VAL_INT)
-		return -EINVAL;
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
